From 4bd5233e4837fbfe4214f5597ec67d06478ea4e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xander Burchartz <210020462+xanderburchartz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:50:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] iOS: main frame

- No desktop menu bar; status bar and iOS status bar follow the color
  scheme.
- Save settings while running: iOS suspends and later kills the app
  without a clean exit.
- Handle rotation (repeated size events, reentry while rebuilding the
  status bar) and new data paths after a reinstall.
- Local help opens through the app, since Safari cannot open files from
  the app bundle.

The iOS implementation lives in the iOS app layer (app/ios/*_ios.cpp in the
opencpn-ios repository); the core only declares and calls it.

All changes are inside #ifdef __OCPN__IOS__; other platforms are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
